# PortfolioDB collector jobs, run by supercronic in the `scheduler` service.
#
# Quote collection only. These jobs fetch third-party web pages (Yahoo), so
# their container holds no API key at all: docker-compose.yml hands the
# `scheduler` service an explicit allowlist instead of .env (audit O-3). The
# jobs that call keyed APIs — the advisor brief and the Financial Datasets
# enrichment — live in docker/crontab-llm and run in `scheduler-llm`. Do not
# add a keyed job here: it would find no key, and the fix is not to give the
# collector one. tools/tests/test_compose_overrides.py keeps the split.
#
# Times are in the container's TZ (PORTFOLIODB_TZ, default UTC). snapshot_prices.py
# exits immediately outside the configured market window (app/market_window.py
# — set it from the Settings page), so the every-5-minutes tick below does not
# need to know the window. Change the window in one place, not here.
#
# Working directory is /app/app so the bare imports resolve the way they do on
# a host; supercronic logs each run's output to the container's stdout.

# Price snapshots — every 5 minutes; the Python guard decides whether to work.
*/5 * * * *   cd /app/app && python snapshot_prices.py

# Market overview benchmarks (index futures, volatility) — every 15 minutes,
# round the clock on weekdays plus Sunday evening, because that is when futures
# trade and the whole point of collecting them is the hours your own market is
# shut. Deliberately NOT gated by the market window, and it records no row in
# snapshot_runs, so Data Health and the MCP cutoff keep meaning "the portfolio's
# prices" — see the comment in snapshot_prices.main.
*/15 * * * 0-5   cd /app/app && python snapshot_prices.py --benchmarks
